=99s received from others. For example, if you sign in to an additional ser=
vice with a Workspace account, we=E2=80=99ll use your Workspace name and pr=
ofile information to identify your account. You can also choose to save you=
r content with Google, things like photos and videos.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>Information we colle=
ct as you use additional services</strong></p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p>Google=E2=80=99s Privacy Policy also describes the=
 information we collect as you use our additional services, which includes:=
</p>
                      <ul>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2 </stro=
ng><strong>Your activity while using additional services</strong>, which in=
cludes things like terms you search for, videos you watch, content and ads =
you view and interact with, voice and audio information when you use audio =
features, purchase activity, and activity on third-party sites and apps tha=
t use our services<a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"=
https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=3Den-US#footnote-chrome-sync" aria-l=
abel=3D"Open the . page in a new tab">.</a></p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2 </stro=
ng><strong>Your apps, browsers &amp; devices</strong>. We collect the info =
about your apps, browser, and devices described above in the core services =
section.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2 </stro=
ng><strong>Your location information</strong>. We collect info about your l=
ocation as determined by various technologies including: GPS, IP address, s=
ensor data from your device, and information about things near your device,=
 such as Wi-Fi access points, cell towers, and Bluetooth-enabled devices. T=
he types of location data we collect depend in part on your device and acco=
unt settings.</p>
                        </li>
                      </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>Why we collect data<=
/strong></p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p>The data we collect in the additional services is =
used across our services to deliver, maintain, and improve our services; de=
velop new services; provide personalized services; measure performance; com=
municate with you; and protect Google, our users, and the public. See the G=
oogle Privacy Policy for more details.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p>Some additional services show ads. But if you=E2=
=80=99re using your Google Workspace for Education account in primary and s=
econdary schools (K-12), we don=E2=80=99t show you personalized ads, which =
means we don=E2=80=99t use information from your account or past activity t=
o target ads. However, we may show ads based on general factors like your s=
earch query, the time of day, or the content of a page you=E2=80=99re readi=
ng.</p>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </section>
              <section id=3D"privacy-police-revamp-sharing" class=3D"_terms=
RichContentWrapper_i3h6k_1 _sectionPadded_i3h6k_5">
                <div class=3D"_cosmeticWrapper_i3h6k_9 _sectionSpacer_i3h6k=
_31"></div>
                <div class=3D"_heading_i3h6k_36 _centered_i3h6k_23">
                  <h3>Sharing your information</h3>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"_container_1r9k7_321 _body_1r9k7_2">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>When you share your =
information</strong></p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p>Your school=E2=80=99s admin may allow students to =
access Google services, such as Google Docs and YouTube, that have features=
 that allow users to share information with others or publicly. For example=
, if you leave a review in Google Play, your name and photo appear next to =
your activity. And if you share a photo with a friend who then makes a copy=
 of it, or shares it again, then that photo may continue to appear in your =
friend=E2=80=99s Google Account even after you remove it from your Google A=
ccount. Remember, when you share information publicly, your content may bec=
ome accessible through search engines, including Google Search.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>When Google shares y=
our information</strong></p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p>As described fully in the Google Privacy Policy an=
d the Google Cloud Privacy Notice, we do not share your personal informatio=
n with companies, organizations, or individuals outside of Google except in=
 the following cases:</p>
                      <ul>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2&nbsp;W=
ith your school=E2=80=99s admin</strong>: Your admin and resellers who mana=
ge your or your organization=E2=80=99s Workspace account will have access t=
o your information. For example, they may be able to:</p>
                          <ul>
                            <li>
                              <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=96=AA&nb=
sp;</strong>View account information, activity and statistics;</p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                              <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=96=AA&nb=
sp;</strong>Change your account password;</p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                              <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=96=AA&nb=
sp;</strong>Suspend or terminate your account access;</p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                              <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=96=AA&nb=
sp;</strong>Access your account information in order to satisfy applicable =
law, regulation, legal process, or enforceable governmental request;</p>
                            </li>
                            <li>
                              <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=96=AA&nb=
sp;</strong>Restrict your ability to delete or edit your information or you=
r privacy settings.</p>
                            </li>
                          </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2&nbsp;W=
ith your consent</strong>: We=E2=80=99ll share personal information outside=
 of Google where we have you or your parent=E2=80=99s consent.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2&nbsp;F=
or external processing</strong>: We share personal information with our aff=
iliates and other trusted third party providers to process it for us as we =
instruct them and in compliance with our&nbsp;<a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"n=
oopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://policies.google.com/privacy" aria-label=
=3D"Open the Privacy Policy page in a new tab">Privacy Policy</a>, the&nbsp=
;<a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://cloud.goo=
gle.com/terms/cloud-privacy-notice" aria-label=3D"Open the Google Cloud Pri=
vacy Notice page in a new tab">Google Cloud Privacy Notice</a>, and any oth=
er appropriate confidentiality and security measures.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2&nbsp;F=
or legal reasons</strong>: We share personal information outside of Google =
if we have a good-faith belief that access, use, preservation or disclosure=
 of the information is reasonably necessary for legal reasons, including co=
mplying with enforceable governmental requests and protecting you and Googl=
e.</p>
                        </li>
                      </ul>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </section>
              <section id=3D"privacy-police-revamp-controls" class=3D"_term=
sRichContentWrapper_i3h6k_1 _sectionPadded_i3h6k_5">
                <div class=3D"_centered_i3h6k_23">
                  <picture><img src=3D"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/IS=
p2RqDBBvZppFqOjZaVVf3_mUkfCdOFzZ9vRtnMGv2AIFxyVFkZ8xb-3IsU04Y25d3HRKI4R43Xi=
8Au5vKaNl6l-XuA5OYBd_PRfQ=3De365-pa-nu-s0-rw" alt=3D"" width=3D"360" height=
=3D"204" loading=3D"lazy"></picture>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"_heading_i3h6k_36 _centered_i3h6k_23">
                  <h3>Your privacy controls</h3>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"_container_1r9k7_321 _body_1r9k7_2">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <p>We provide a variety of controls that enable stude=
nts and parents to make meaningful choices about how information is used in=
 Google services. Depending on the settings enabled by your school=E2=80=99=
s admin, students&nbsp; can use settings like&nbsp;<a target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://myactivity.google.com/activitycont=
rols" aria-label=3D"Open the Google activity controls page in a new tab">Go=
ogle activity controls</a>, to manage their privacy and information. We pro=
vide additional information for parents, students, and admins in the&nbsp;<=
a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://www.google.=
com/edu/trust/" aria-label=3D"Open the Google Workspace for Education Priva=
cy Center page in a new tab">Google Workspace for Education Privacy Center<=
/a>.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                      <p>School admins also have service controls that can =
allow you to manage personal information, including limiting its further co=
llection or use. If you or your child has a Google Workspace for Education =
account, contact your admin to:</p>
                      <ul>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2 </stro=
ng>access your personal information</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2 </stro=
ng>limit access to features or services</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                          <p class=3D"strong-item"><strong>=E2=80=A2 </stro=
ng>delete personal information in services or delete your entire account</p=
>
                        </li>
                      </ul>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </section>
              <section id=3D"privacy-police-revamp-about" class=3D"_termsRi=
chContentWrapper_i3h6k_1 _sectionPadded_i3h6k_5">
                <div class=3D"_cosmeticWrapper_i3h6k_9 _bgGrey_i3h6k_19"></=
div>
                <div class=3D"_heading_i3h6k_36 _centered_i3h6k_23">
                  <h3>About this policy</h3>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"_container_1r9k7_321 _body_1r9k7_2">
                  <ul>
                    <li>
                      <p>This Notice is intended to provide the key informa=
tion about our collection and use of data for Google Workspace for Educatio=
n users, and is consistent with the Google Privacy Policy and the Google Cl=
oud Privacy Notice. In cases that specific commitments differ, this privacy=
 notice takes precedence followed by the Google Cloud Privacy Notice and th=
e Google Privacy Policy. For example, the Google Privacy Policy has a descr=
iption of personalized ads that isn=E2=80=99t relevant to Google Workspace =
for Education users in primary and secondary schools (K-12), and this notic=
e clarifies that we don=E2=80=99t show personalized ads to those students.<=
/p>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </section>
